      "prior_exact_reason": "Fresh row-specific assessment supports the monohydrate-to-melezitose form-of relation. The inspected monohydrate InChI minus its one water component equals both PubChem CID 92817 and active CHEBI:6731 exactly, including stereochemistry. MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections 1-3 require NARROW_MATCH to emit skos:broadMatch with a B1 handle; this is neither exact parent identity nor an ontology subclass claim. The actual parent row publishes no other tokens.",
      "prior_proposal_action": "PROPOSE_RETAIN_QUALIFIED_SUPPORT",
      "reason": "Current license-corrected publication assessment: I have read the complete current assertion, owner, claim-specific captured authority and preserved negative conditions. The project-authored header now correctly states CC BY4.0; this metadata correction grants no chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Current claim-specific conclusion and its complete inherited scope: Current requalification after the publisher-only repair: the complete assertion, owner, raw authority scope and original negative conditions remain scientifically unchanged. I retain the following claim-specific conclusion; fresh producer/diagnostic receipts do not grant new chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Captured ChEBI CHEBI:6731 declares ['melezitose']; formula ['C18H32O16']; charge ['0']. Assess the named concept and predicate against the current owner, not against an assumed source procurement identity. Current captured target/source declarations corroborate this named material and the actual predicate within the retained qualified scientific scope. The historical assessment is context, not substituted primary authority. The complete current row, owner and all changed metadata/aliases are assessed here; source occurrence approval remains separate. Retained scope restriction from earlier assessment: Fresh row-specific assessment supports the monohydrate-to-melezitose form-of relation. The inspected monohydrate InChI minus its one water component equals both PubChem CID 92817 and active CHEBI:6731 exactly, including stereochemistry. MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections 1-3 require NARROW_MATCH to emit skos:broadMatch with a B1 handle; this is neither exact parent identity nor an ontology subclass claim. The actual parent row publishes no other tokens. The typed skos:broadMatch relation is not identity, replacement or subclass_of. Its form, salt, hydrate, preparation or similarity scope remains explicit. All prior source tokens and nonempty comments survive the native proposed row. Mapping date is the latest recorded owner event, not new literature acquisition; deterministic confidence is not a calibrated probability. Cleared validation stamps remain in exact beforeimages and are not claimed as current checks. Canonical installation only; no production release, source binding, role approval, identity collapse, subclass inference or KG rebuild. Full row beforeimages, owner evidence, suppressions and original W01/W09 history remain linked. Current direct origin-capture reading: Read raw PubChem CID16217716 C18H34O17 and its explicit single H2O component, CID92817 C18H32O16, and current captured CHEBI6731 identical parent InChI including stereochemistry. CAS10030-67-8 is the hydrate scope, distinct from parentCAS597-12-6. Original CultureBotHT explicitly names monohydrate. CHEBI183824 is a conflicting stereoisomer (10+ versus target10-) and does not replace the parent. This supports assessing the existing typed hydrate-of broad mapping, never exact parent identity or subclass. Full current native selection and separate review are still pending."
