      "prior_exact_reason": "Keep the NCI-defined B1/B2 mixture. CAS 1404-26-8 annotates this mixture; CHEBI:8309 and CAS 4135-11-9 denote B1. Neither B1 nor sulfate is equivalent to this record.",
      "prior_proposal_action": "PROPOSE_RETAIN_QUALIFIED_SUPPORT",
      "reason": "Current license-corrected publication assessment: I have read the complete current assertion, owner, claim-specific captured authority and preserved negative conditions. The project-authored header now correctly states CC BY4.0; this metadata correction grants no chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Current claim-specific conclusion and its complete inherited scope: Current requalification after the publisher-only repair: the complete assertion, owner, raw authority scope and original negative conditions remain scientifically unchanged. I retain the following claim-specific conclusion; fresh producer/diagnostic receipts do not grant new chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Captured ontology declaration: {\"rdfs:label\": [\"Polymyxin B\"], \"IAO:0000115\": [\"A mixture of the polypeptides polymyxins B1 and B2, both obtained from Bacillus polymyxa strains, with antimicrobial activity. Polymyxin B exerts its antimicrobial effect through its cationic detergent action on cell membranes. Specifically, this antibiotic binds to the negatively charged site in the lipopolysaccharide layer of the bacterial cell membrane via electrostatic affinity with the positively charged amino groups in the cyclic peptide portion. Subsequently, the fatty acid portion of polymyxin B dissolves in the hydrophobic region of the bacterial cell membrane. This results in an alteration in cell membrane structure, disruption of cell wall integrity and an increase in permeability for water and molecules. This will eventually lead to bacterial cell death.\"], \"oio:hasExactSynonym\": [\"POLYMYXIN B\", \"Polymyxin B\"]} Current captured target/source declarations corroborate this named material and the actual predicate within the retained qualified scientific scope. The historical assessment is context, not substituted primary authority. The complete current row, owner and all changed metadata/aliases are assessed here; source occurrence approval remains