      "prior_exact_reason": "The actual sodium perchlorate monohydrate row is supported as a form-of skos:broadMatch to CHEBI:132103 sodium perchlorate. Archived PubChem CID516899 has one water component in addition to the sodium/perchlorate structure represented by the water-free ChEBI parent. The parent row has empty other and validation_method cells, resolving the old hydrate-CAS alias leakage and providing an explicit asymmetric relation instead of inherited closeMatch approval. This supports the bounded relation, not global exhaustion of exact ontology alternatives.",
      "prior_proposal_action": "PROPOSE_RETAIN_QUALIFIED_SUPPORT",
      "reason": "Current license-corrected publication assessment: I have read the complete current assertion, owner, claim-specific captured authority and preserved negative conditions. The project-authored header now correctly states CC BY4.0; this metadata correction grants no chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Current claim-specific conclusion and its complete inherited scope: Current requalification after the publisher-only repair: the complete assertion, owner, raw authority scope and original negative conditions remain scientifically unchanged. I retain the following claim-specific conclusion; fresh producer/diagnostic receipts do not grant new chemistry, source identity, role or release support. Captured ChEBI CHEBI:132103 declares ['sodium perchlorate']; formula ['ClO4.Na']; charge ['0']. Assess the named concept and predicate against the current owner, not against an assumed source procurement identity. Current captured target/source declarations corroborate this named material and the actual predicate within the retained qualified scientific scope. The historical assessment is context, not substituted primary authority. The complete current row, owner and all changed metadata/aliases are assessed here; source occurrence approval remains separate. Retained scope restriction from earlier assessment: The actual sodium perchlorate monohydrate row is supported as a form-of skos:broadMatch to CHEBI:132103 sodium perchlorate. Archived PubChem CID516899 has one water component in addition to the sodium/perchlorate structure represented by the water-free ChEBI parent. The parent row has empty other and validation_method cells, resolving the old hydrate-CAS alias leakage and providing an explicit asymmetric relation instead of inherited closeMatch approval. This supports the bounded relation, not global exhaustion of exact ontology alternatives. The typed skos:broadMatch relation is not identity, replacement or subclass_of. Its form, salt, hydrate